      "0": "Screenshots show the Google Flights interface with origin New Delhi (DEL), destination Bengaluru (BLR), trip type Round trip, cabin Economy, and passenger count shown as “1 passenger” / “1 Adults.” One state shows the date picker explicitly indicating Sep 15, 2026 as departure and Sep 18, 2026 as return, with the Done button text confirming those dates; later states show a results page where the page text and query context indicate departing 2026-09-15 and returning 2026-09-18. Some intermediate DOM states don’t display the selected date values in the input fields, so date compliance may rely on the later results-page evidence rather than the earlier form-only states.",
      "1": "The Stops filter UI is visible, including a “Nonstop only” option in a Stops dialog. One results-page state shows the filter chip reading “Nonstop, Stops, Selected” and “All filters, 1 filter selected,” which is explicit evidence that a nonstop filter is applied at that moment. Additionally, the visible flight cards carry a “Nonstop” label; however, not all screenshots show an explicit checked/selected attribute on the “Nonstop only” radio itself, so the clearest confirmation is the filter-chip state plus nonstop-labeled results.",
      "2": "In the visible results list, the lowest round-trip fare displayed is €154, and there are exactly three visible options at that same lowest price (all labeled €154 round trip). Other visible options are higher priced (€159, €160, €161), so selecting those three €154 options matches the “three lowest visible” requirement via a tie at the minimum price point.",
      "3": "Each of the three €154 options visibly includes: airline (IndiGo), an outbound departure and arrival time window (e.g., 3:00 AM–5:55 AM, 8:45 PM–11:40 PM, 10:00 PM–12:55 AM +1), duration (2 hr 55 min), and the round-trip fare (€154 round trip), plus “Nonstop.” The results cards shown are for ‘departing flights’ and do not display return-leg departure times/durations in the visible list, so any requirement to report return timing would need an explicit note that return details are not shown in the visible cards.",
      "4": "The screenshots where results are visible show three lowest-priced options tied on price and duration, differing mainly by outbound departure/arrival time (very early morning vs evening vs late-night with after-midnight arrival). This supports making a schedule-based recommendation among price-equal options without needing booking steps; only “Select flight” buttons are visible, not a checkout/booking flow. The visible evidence supports reasoning based on outbound schedule only, since return schedule details are not shown in the cards."
